#
# IEEE 802.1X port authentication.
#
# hostapd is the authenticator, in its wired mode, and carries the RADIUS
# client; wpasupplicant provides wpa_supplicant, needed to test a port from the
# supplicant side and useful on a box that is itself authenticating upstream.
# Both come from Debian -- neither is a DANOS package.
#
# They were absent until 2608. The dataplane change that made 802.1X possible
# was the EAPOL punt in ether_forward_process(); with it in place, EAP-MD5
# completes over a dataplane port, but only with these installed, and an
# earlier verification run reported an authentication failure that was really
# a missing binary.
#
# Checked on a box where both were installed by hand, because the two behave
# differently and only one of them is harmless by default:
#
#   hostapd.service          masked    -- installing it starts nothing
#   wpa_supplicant.service   enabled   -- would start at boot on every image
#
# A supplicant daemon running on every DANOS box is not something packaging a
# feature should introduce, so hooks/live/16-mask-wpa-supplicant.chroot masks
# it to match hostapd's posture: present, configured by an operator, started
# deliberately.
#
hostapd
wpasupplicant
